Quick Setup

   1. Move Binary:

   1     sudo mv gclone /usr/local/bin/

   2. Configuration:
      Create ~/.config/rclone/rclone.conf with this content:

   1     [gc]
   2     type = drive
   3     scope = drive
   4     # Path to one JSON file (required as base)
   5     service_account_file = /path/to/gclone/accounts/1.json
   6     # Folder with ALL your JSON files (gclone will rotate these)
   7     service_account_file_path = /path/to/gclone/accounts/
   8     root_folder_id = root
      Make sure to put your .json service account files in your chosen accounts directory.

   3. Systemd Service:
      I've already created the service file at systemd/gclone.service. Activate it now:

   1     mkdir -p ~/gdrive
   2     sudo cp bin/gclone-mount /usr/local/bin/gclone-mount
   3     sudo cp systemd/gclone.service /etc/systemd/system/gclone.service
   4     # Open it to double check paths: sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/gclone.service
   5     sudo systemctl daemon-reload
   6     sudo systemctl enable gclone
   7     sudo systemctl start gclone

  Optional selective sync:
   1     cp config/gclone-selective-sync.txt.template ~/.config/rclone/gclone-selective-sync.txt
   2     # Example contents:
   3     # + /Research/**
   4     # + /Teaching/**
   5     # - *
   6     sudo systemctl restart gclone

  Optional selective sync GUI:
   1     chmod +x bin/gclone-selective-sync-ui
   2     ./bin/gclone-selective-sync-ui --mountpoint /path/to/your/mount
   3     # Open http://127.0.0.1:43123 and save your folder selection
   4     sudo systemctl restart gclone

  Key Features of your new "Dropbox":
   * Infinite Upload: Automatically bypasses the 750GB/day limit by rotating service accounts.
   * On-Demand Sync: Files only download when you click them, saving local space.
   * Background Upload: Changes you save are uploaded in the background via the VFS cache.
   * Auto-Start: Always available on boot via systemd.

  You can check the status at any time with systemctl status gclone or view logs with tail -f ~/.config/rclone/gclone.log.
